  "release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-declared-seed-compiler-and-native-observations",
  :record
  "- [ ] `release/remaining-tasks-and-evidence/implement-declared-seed-compiler-and-native-observations` Implement declared seed compiler and native observations\n\nStatus: Open\n\nEvidence baseline: [Seed compiler contract](../../docs/phase-15-bootstrap-and-self-hosting/204-boot2-seed-compiler-design.md)\n\nClosing evidence: Retain existing seed/native implementations and bounded historical receipts at their original scope; reuse applicable evidence without treating a new task interface as missing implementation or promoting historical acceptance. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/native-carrier-header: Implement unary bootstrap-native-carrier-header only for compiler-artifact meta/JVM plans, returning exactly kind, metadata-present?, extent, metric, child0 and child1. Unknown or inaccessible observations return the six-slot unsupported header with unknown metrics nil. Check every operand and nested receiver by exact native class before native observation. Cover nil, Boolean, Character, Byte/Short/Integer/Long, String/Symbol/Keyword, the declared native maps/set/vector/List/Cons/SubVector and BigInt/BigInteger/Ratio/BigDecimal/Float/Double contours. Preserve the source's UTF16 spelling metrics, native null-name Boolean, integer absolute-magnitude bits, checked BigInt backing, separate Ratio numerator/denominator without GCD/printing, fixed Float/Double carrier widths and BigDecimal unscaled-bits plus widened signed scale. For PersistentArrayMap, require an available non-null even physical array and return length/2 before metadata/count; reject odd/null/inaccessible backing as unsupported, including a HashSet's backing map. Preserve TreeMap default-versus-foreign comparator identity without invoking it, List raw head/tail without forcing Cons, and SubVector raw backing/start/widened end-minus-start extent without backing methods. HashSet uses only the fixed checked impl field. Construct only the selected returned header, with no unconditional fallback tuple. Exercise wrong arity/context, foreign/spoofed classes or nested numeric/Keyword receivers, inaccessible/odd/null backing, comparator callbacks, metadata callbacks, Cons forcing and SubVector delegated methods. Unsupported results have unsupported kind and nil in all remaining slots, never zero for an unknown metric. Symbol child0 is false for a null name and true for an empty or other non-null name, with child1 nil. Metadata is only a native-class-checked presence Boolean and is never walked or returned; use no Number coercion, numeric normalization or equality. Require L2-BUILTIN-ARITY or L2-BUILTIN-ERROR without operand rendering as specified; unsupported observation never implies DATA illegality. No equality/hashing/rendering/traversal, general reflection, caller-selected fields, module opening, Unsafe, denial retry or security bypass is permitted. Fixed field-access denial stays sticky; its Delay/Atom/Field state caches only fixed infrastructure including denial, never DATA or DATA validity. Cold resolution and accessor initialization remain audited host mechanisms. Headers do not confer provenance, admission or child validity. Keep the ABI outside ordinary Core/C5 catalogs and authenticated-source admission, and invalidate affected seed fingerprints without renewing old migration evidence. Required outputs: six-slot result corpus for every declared native contour and numeric extrema; callback/non-forcing and exact-class negative reports; sticky-denial/physical-backing and arity/context diagnostic fixtures; seed TCB and ordinary-export exclusion records. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/native-reference-identity: Implement binary bootstrap-native-identical? in compiler-artifact meta/JVM plans with compiler-artifact kind and flag. Evaluate each operand once, then return Boolean native JVM reference sameness, including two null references, while distinguishing ancestor cycles from repeated shared values. Reject wrong arity/context with L2-BUILTIN-ARITY/L2-BUILTIN-ERROR without rendering. Instrument operands so equality/hash/metadata/render/traversal callbacks never run. Expose no address or stable token and grant no DATA/comparison legality; interning or boxing does not establish language identity. Keep ordinary Core/C5 catalogs and source admissions unchanged and retain the implementation/allowlist as seed TCB without migration credit. Required outputs: same/distinct/null/shared/cyclic reference result fixtures; once-evaluation and zero-callback controls; arity/context and no-export diagnostics/records. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/native-symbol-units: Implement unary bootstrap-symbol-utf16-unit-count only in compiler-artifact meta/JVM kind/flag/module context for exactly native clojure.lang.Symbol. Count native name and namespace String UTF16 lengths with a slash for every non-null namespace, including empty; null names add zero with null namespace and four literal null units with present namespace. Preserve empty names, supplementary pairs and unpaired surrogates, using arithmetic wide enough for two maximal String lengths and a separator. Evaluate the operand once before ABI checks. Use exact-class, wrong-context and wrong-arity fixtures with L2-BUILTIN-ERROR/L2-BUILTIN-ARITY without rendering; exclude user Named callbacks, interning/hash/metadata/UTF8 conversion. This is neither Unicode validation nor scalar counting, source authentication, C5 evidence or a public Core/library export. Record affected seed TCB/fingerprint invalidation without renewing historical migration or self-hosting evidence. Required outputs: UTF16 name/namespace/null/surrogate and representability fixtures; once-evaluation/no-callback controls; arity/context/class diagnostic and export-exclusion records. Bootstrap criterion bootstrap/seed-subset: Execute the declared minimal seed reader/syntax/core/namespace/macro/type/effect/MIR/diagnostic/backend/artifact-manifest surface against its upstream language contracts. Publish implemented and excluded documents/features/profiles, host dependencies and runtime assumptions, stable diagnostic report and subset conformance; emit the seed executable/backend artifact and manifest with source/compiler/backend/environment/dependency hashes and metadata sufficient to compare stage1. The seed remains an auditable temporary subset, not an alternate language definition. Accepted subset programs must emit real declared artifacts; undeclared features, unsupported profiles/forms (including warning-only acceptance), missing provenance, unstable/missing diagnostic codes, untracked host dependencies or upstream semantic mismatch must reject with BOOT2001-BOOT2006 as applicable. Ordinary development results do not confer seed retirement; explicit exclusions limit this seed surface and do not remove full-language obligations. Required outputs: seed executable/backend artifact and source-bound manifest; supported/excluded subset and host/runtime trust reports; accepted/rejected subset fixtures, stable BOOT2 diagnostics and stage1 comparison metadata.",
